  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Libretro core .dlls, packaged so they land in the AppX at
         InstalledLocation()\cores\*.dll; QuickMenu (ui\quick_menu.cpp)
         enumerates exactly that folder via Package::Current().
         InstalledLocation().GetFolderAsync(L"cores"), and LibretroHost::
         LoadCore's LoadPackagedLibrary call requires the module to already
         be package content rather than an arbitrary sideloaded path (see
         that function's own doc comment). Deliberately <None>, not
         <Content>: this is a native C++/WinRT UWP project, and its
         packaging targets never picked up a <Content Include> item at all;
         confirmed by it being absent even from x64\Debug\...\
         unfiltered.layout.resfiles, the raw pre-filter list the AppX
         layout step builds from. <None> + DeploymentContent=true is the
         form these targets actually recognize (matches how VS itself
         writes it when you set a file's "Content" property to "Yes" via
         Solution Explorer in a C++ project). Add one entry per core .dll
         placed under the project's cores\ folder. -->
    <None Include="cores\mupen64plus_next_libretro.dll">
      <DeploymentContent>true</DeploymentContent>
    </None>
    <None Include="cores\fceumm_libretro.dll">
